WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
Take a salt of iron.

2
00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:05.500
Look at its formula:
not one hydrogen atom.

3
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.140
Dissolve it in water, and the
solution looks yellow-brown.

4
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.720
Now measure its pH.

5
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.320
About pH 2.

6
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.400
The solution is acidic.

7
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.120
Acidic means hydrogen
ions in the solution.

8
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.540
But the salt had none to give.

9
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:25.220
So how can a metal salt with no hydrogen
in its formula give away hydrogen ions?

10
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.300
In this mission, you'll meet the
shades of metal ions in water:

11
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.460
blue copper, pale green iron, and more.

12
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.640
Then you'll add hydroxide, drop by drop,
and watch a solid appear in the tube.

13
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:41.400
Your mission: explain where
the hydrogen ions come from.